# Illusionary Mask's effect outlives the Mask (the ruling): Bot1 casts Caelorna, Coral Tyrant (a 0/8) face down with {U}{U}
# spent on X, and on turn 2 Bot2 destroys the Mask with Shatter, then Lightning Bolts the face-down 2/2. The 3 damage would be
# dealt to it: instead it is turned face up and is dealt the damage (CR 614.1, 614.6) - as the 0/8, so it survives with 3
# damage marked. Not prevented, not dealt to a 2/2: the face-down 2/2 would have died. "A creature card" is one: Coral Eel's
# {1}{U} could be paid too, but not with Caelorna as well. Damage dealt to Bot1 meanwhile is no damage to it or by it, and it stays face down.
# Cast face down it has no way to be turned up for its mana cost (it is no manifested card, CR 701.40b, 708.2a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Illusionary Mask
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Caelorna, Coral Tyrant
Coral Eel
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
